Appendix 3:

 
              Command Line Parameters for 4D-BBS V2.86

     All parameters are proceeded with a / or - and should be spaced
apart BETWEEN THE PARAMTERS.  NO spaces should be between the - or /
and the actual command itself.  CLPS CAN NOT be stacked by using a
single - or / with multiple commands.  A # should be replaced by a
numerical value, and a $ should be replaced by a character string. In
the event a space is needed for a parameter enclose JUST that parameter,
including the / within spaces. The commands ARE case sensitive.

   Note: $ = String		# = Nummber	! = Numeric Switch (0=off, 1=on)

Param Description                                       Example
----- ------------------------------------------------  --------------

A!    Enter ARexx Port Servor Mode, Wait for Commands.  /A

a$    ARexx Port Name. Defaults to "4D-BBS".            /aBBS

B#    Carrier Baud rate of a /o call (use with /b).     /B2400

b#    W/O  /o parameter: Lock Serial Port at rate.      /b19200
      With /o parameter: Serial Baud rate for call.     /b9600

C#    Number of Last Callers to keep track of           /C5

c#    Number of Colors in Bitplanes. Colors = 2^c.      /c2

D$    Filename of Directories datafile.                 /DBBS:NewDirs.Dat

d#    Hangup Method. 0=No Hangup, 1=DTR, 2=+++,,,ATH    /d1

f$    Font to use with 4D-BBS. Defaults to 4D-BBS.      /fIBMFONT

G$    Config file for 4D-BBS to use.                    /DS:4D.Config

h!    Reset to SystemHighBaud After every caller.       /h0

H!    Hide screen and don't make active when starting.  /H1

I!    Open 4D-BBS in iconified mode instead of full     /I1
      screen.

L#    Number of Screen Lines to use (#>32=Interlace).   /L50

M!    Whether to use Pull down menus or not.            /M0

m$    Alternate Modem Response file to use.             /mBBS:MTModem.Dat

N$    UserName if using /o.                             "/NJone Doe"

o!    Normal Wait modem(0) or Logon once remote(1).     /o1
os    Logon once local with out a waiting screen.       /os or /o2

P$    User's Password if using /o.                      "/PNOT Tell" 

Q$    AutoDetect mode (and optional CONNECT string).    /QCONNECT 

q$    Fax Modem (and optional Fax Connect String).      /qFAX

R$    Reliable mode (and optional Reliable string).     /RARQ          

r!    Use XPRS (1) or RZ/SZ external programs (1).      /r1

S$    Alternate Default annouce string.                 "/S Going Down, Sorry"

s$    Alternate Serial Device Name to use.              /sSerial0.Device

T#    Time added or subtracted with F7/F8 or menu.      /T15

t#    Inactivity timeout before auto-logoff.            /t8

U#    Secs per K uploaded reqarded to users.            /U5 

u#    Alternate Serial Device Unit Number to use.       /u1

V#    Verbose setting of system information.            /V4

v!    Voice talking of User's actions                   /v1
